## A general category with unresolved modifier scope

Input:
```json
{
  "A": {
    "subject": "Red geometry models",
    "meaning": "Red geometry models are solid physical geometry models that are themselves red."
  },
  "B": {
    "subject": "Display shapes",
    "meaning": "Display shapes are solid physical geometry models restricted to red cubes and spheres. These shape and color descriptions apply to the models themselves."
  }
}
```

Output:
```json
{
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "A_contains_B",
      "question": "Could information about an entirely blue sphere model satisfy B, Display shapes, while escaping A, Red geometry models?"
    },
    {
      "id": "B_contains_A",
      "question": "Could information about a red cone model satisfy A, Red geometry models, while escaping B, Display shapes, under either reading?"
    }
  ],
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "A_contains_B",
      "justification": "Red can modify both cubes and spheres, or only cubes. Under the first reading, every qualifying B model is red, and B's kind connections concern qualifying A models. Under the second, B also admits entirely blue sphere models unrelated to red models or their production and evaluation; information solely about such a sphere escapes A. The candidate's admission and the directional outcome therefore depend on unresolved modifier scope, rather than merely an absent condition.",
      "answer": null
    },
    {
      "question_id": "B_contains_A",
      "justification": "A red cone model satisfies A. Both readings of B restrict its models to cubes or spheres. Information solely about an independent cone concerns neither a qualifying B model nor its properties, composition, production, occurrences or evaluation. Shared color or geometric subject matter alone does not establish coverage.",
      "answer": "A description of the shape and red coloring of a standalone solid cone model, unrelated to cube or sphere models or their production or evaluation."
    }
  ],
  "relation": "uncertain",
  "reason": "B's modifier scope leaves A's coverage unresolved; A admits red cone models outside either reading of B."
}
```
